[version]
1.5.2
[date]
2026-10-21
[whatsnew]
- FIXED: Terminal (sh.lua) commands now stay inside their window!
  - Old: sh.lua used Kernel.exec() for each command (ls, cat, etc.)
    which created new processes that didn't inherit term.redirect
  - New: sh.lua runs commands IN-PROCESS via load() + pcall()
  - This means term.redirect (set by window manager) is inherited
  - Command output stays inside the window, not on full screen
- NEW: GUI on external Monitor (bin/gui-to-monitor.lua)
  - Launch the entire desktop on a Monitor block
  - 'gui-to-monitor <side>' or 'gui-to-monitor --list'
  - All windows, menus, apps appear on the monitor
  - Input comes from the computer's terminal
- NEW: Paint on external Monitor
  - 'paint --monitor <side>' to draw on a Monitor block
  - Touch the monitor to draw (monitor_touch events)
  - See your artwork on the big screen
- Background commands still use Kernel.exec (can't dofile in bg)
[/whatsnew]
[files]
bin/sh.lua
bin/gui-to-monitor.lua
usr/bin/paint.lua
installer.lua
latest_update.upd
[/files]
